@tigattack Thanks for the creating this issue report. The MAC address is currently checked before finishing the setup process. If the MAC address cannot be read (e.g. MC server running in different subnet as HA) then it will fail. This is a known limitation. But you should still be able to add the server with the hostname (hostname:port). In that case the MAC address is not required.

Or maybe the PR from @cyberjacob gets accepted. In that case you can just wait for it. But currently is not clear yet if removing the MAC address check is allowed or not. We are waiting for further input from the HA team.

Or didn't I understand your issue? In that case please give some more details. Thanks in advance.

@elmurato You've understood my issue correctly. I'm now attempting to add the server with hostname:port, but this fails with the following error
>  Failed to connect to server. Please check the host and port and try again. Also ensure that you are running at least Minecraft version 1.7 on your server. 

I can connect to the server with my Minecraft client using the same hostname:port with no issues, so the problem doesn't appear to be server availability.
